{"pair_id":"r2val-pair-potassium-lsss-safety","action_label":"PAIR_PRESERVE","topic":"potassium target plus LSSS safety scope","old_evidence":{"document_id":"who-potassium-2012","edition":"2012","published_at":"2012-12-25","official_url":"https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789241504829","official_pdf_url":"https://iris.who.int/server/api/core/bitstreams/8516dcd5-49a9-486e-890b-48471468a5bb/content","local_path":"experiments/version_aware_rag/data/sources_v4/who/who_potassium_2012.pdf","source_sha256":"c2b221752f81604faf748e1a33420db8bdb8b7eb3b8f33ac8310c712982c4d0d","page_number":10,"chunk_id":"who-potassium-2012-page-10-pass-1-d7bcb1c747","text":"WHO suggests a potassium intake of at least 90 mmol/day (3510 mg/day) for adults (conditional recommendation2 ).","text_sha256":"c821727c85bfe9ff55047d92636a37a051de3d695a2efea76ecea3a41325876e","extraction_method":"frozen_v4_pdf_chunk_exact_substring"},"current_evidence":{"document_id":"who-lsss-2025","edition":"2025","published_at":"2025-01-27","official_url":"https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240105591","official_pdf_url":"https://iris.who.int/server/api/core/bitstreams/31fad89a-d7c2-450c-9b74-cd2a8752e60f/content","local_path":"experiments/version_aware_rag/data/sources_v4/who/who_lower_sodium_salt_substitutes_2025.pdf","source_sha256":"e7111969908bbf588c20b457b6f5f26ce16e6d9e023e7e179d8a9c1b54a318a0","page_number":12,"chunk_id":"who-lsss-2025-page-12-pass-0-a257aa450a","text":"This recommendation is intended for adults (not pregnant women or children) in general populations, excluding individuals with kidney impairments or with other circumstances or conditions that might compromise potassium excretion.","text_sha256":"ace776146f9479f6649c0bc0ed25070dae8ad697b7d49a0198f0e7e0bf1712fe","extraction_method":"frozen_v4_pdf_chunk_exact_substring"},"reviewer_rationale":"The general potassium target and newer exclusion conditions are jointly required for safe advice.","reviewer_id":"codex-gpt5-primary-reviewer